Review the diff at bench/iterations/006/reviews/iter-006-outcome.diff — three incremental fixes to the agent loop's RunOutcome aggregation (the outcome-accuracy findings deferred from iter-004, done WITHOUT a full TurnController extraction). (#7) router.recordSuccess (momentum) moved from the success block (which runs BEFORE Phase-7 tool-nudge and Phase-3 verify recursion) to the true terminal just before the done yield, guarded by runOutcome.status===succeeded, so a nudged/verify-failed turn no longer credits momentum and doesn't double-count with the recursive child. (#8) thisAttempt (the current ModelAttemptOutcome) is now threaded into _attemptsSoFar for the nudge and verify recursions too (previously only fallback), so the terminal aggregate carries every invocation. (#9) RunOutcome.recovery changed from a single enum to an ordered array; each recursion appends its action (fallback/tool_nudge/verification_retry) into _recoverySoFar and the terminal appends forced_synthesis, so fallback-then-synthesis records both in order instead of erasing the fallback. Verify each is correct: no double-counting, no lost/duplicated attempts, recovery order accurate, no new races. Output ONLY JSON: {"fixes":[{"id":7|8|9,"status":"resolved"|"not-resolved","note":string}],"new_P0_P1":[]}
